titutional symptoms argue against de novo AML in favor of a chronic process?", "summary": "The subacute onset favors a chronic process over de novo AML, which typically presents more acutely. This weakens support for de novo AML and increases the likelihood of chronic conditions such as CML or myeloproliferative neoplasms."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the combination of constitutional symptoms and normal physical exam (lack of splenomegaly) argue against CML blast crisis as the most likely diagnosis?", "summary": "The absence of splenomegaly and a more subacute clinical course are atypical for CML blast crisis, which tends to present with more aggressive symptoms and physical signs. This weakens the support for blast crisis."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of a documented prior myelodysplastic condition or genetic abnormalities disfavor MDS as a diagnosis?", "summary": "The lack of prior MDS or known genetic abnormalities weakens the plausibility of MDS with excess blasts as an explanation. This provides weak evidence against the diagnosis."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the lack of specific genetic markers (e.g., t(8;21), inv(16)) and absence of blasts in the differential disfavor AML with recurrent abnormalities?", "summary": "AML with known recurrent abnormalities would typically present with blasts in the peripheral blood and specific cytogenetic findings. The absence of these features disfavors this subtype."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of marked erythrocytosis or abnormal red blood cell morphology disfavor polycythemia vera as a diagnosis?", "summary": "The absence of marked erythrocytosis or abnormal red blood cell morphology reduces the likelihood of polycythemia vera, as these are hallmark findings for the condition."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly or other stigmata of myelofibr